#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:1 src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Backup & Restore"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:9
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad ships scripts in package installations for backup & restore which you "
"can use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These scripts do not come with any warranty and may not work in your "
"specific\n"
"use case. This depends on the configuration and installation type of your\n"
"instance.\n"
"\n"
"You should always regularly test and review the functionality! If the "
"script\n"
"functionality or scope is not working for your cases, feel free to copy "
"these\n"
"to a independent location and adjust the scripts as needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "There are some limitations you should know:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "These scripts won't work in container based installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "They only work for PostgreSQL installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "The backup is always a full dump (no incremental backup)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Partial backup and restore (e.g. only specific data like tickets,users) is "
"not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switching database system is not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "System settings (like environment variables) are not backed up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Restore to an older Zammad version is not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Do not restore backup files from custom scripts with the provided scripts by "
"Zammad. This might cause problems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The scripts are located in `/opt/zammad/contrib/backup`. The following files "
"are relevant:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "Backup configuration file: `config.dist`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "Script for backing up your data: `zammad_backup.sh`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "Script for restoring your data: `zammad_restore.sh`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To execute a backup based on the default configuration, follow the steps "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Copy the `config.dist` file to `config`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change default parameters in the config file if needed. See [Backup "
"Configuration](#backup-config-parametersbackup-config-parameters) for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Stop Zammad `systemctl stop zammad`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Execute `/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_backup.sh` (as `root` or `zammad` "
"user)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Backup Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can find details about the configuration parameters with default values "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:60
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`BACKUP_DIR` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"/var/tmp/zammad_backup\"/>\n"
": Location where the script writes the backup files to. The directory will "
"be\n"
"  created if it does not exist. Make sure you have enough space because "
"the\n"
"  script writes full dumps.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`HOLD_DAYS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"10\"/>\n"
": Define how many days the backup script should keep old backups. This "
"value\n"
"  contains a 60 minutes grace period (e.g. 10 days plus 1 hour) for safety\n"
"  reasons. Old backups are removed before creating the a new backup.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Examples:\n"
"  - `1` will keep backups of the last 25 hours\n"
"  - `-1` will remove all available backups (except the new one)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`FULL_FS_DUMP` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"yes\"/>\n"
": - `yes`: the backup includes also application files.\n"
"  - `no`: the backup includes only user data.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In any case, it includes the Zammad database and the attachments, if you\n"
"  stored them in the file system. If you are in doubt, set this to no.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:79
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``DEBUG`` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"no\"/>\n"
": Setting this option to `yes` will output useful debug messages.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This option potentially returns sensitive information to standard output! "
"Do\n"
"  not use this option in production environments or ensure to turn it off "
"after\n"
"  testing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:85
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Restore Backups"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Important Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please read the following information carefully before starting to restore "
"your data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This section is **not** about **migrating from one host to another**. You "
"can find instructions about this topic in the [next "
"section](#migrate-to-a-new-host)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid "This guide expects a fully installed Zammad version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid "It also expects you to restore Zammad on the same host and Zammad version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The restore process stops & restarts Zammad. Therefore you have to run the "
"restore script with appropriate permissions (e.g. as root)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid "PostgreSQL based installations will drop and re-create the database!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"At least twice the backed up Zammad instance size of free storage is "
"required. If you have the dump only, factor 3 could be a good number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your scenario is different as described above, please consult the\n"
"[Zammad "
"Community](https://community.zammad.org/c/trouble-running-zammad-this-is-your-place/5) "
"or consider\n"
"[paid support "
"options](https://zammad.com/en/services/professional-services).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:108
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy Backup Files to a Fitting Location"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:112
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Ensure that the user you're using for restoration is allowed to read the "
"backup files and to write to `/opt/zammad/`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid "The Zammad backup consists of two files. They are named like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<timestamp>_zammad_db.psql.gz\n"
"<timestamp>_zammad_files.tar.gz\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:121
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"There are also two symlinks in your backup directory pointing to the newest "
"backup created:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"latest_zammad_db.psql.gz\n"
"latest_zammad_files.tar.gz\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:129
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Copy them to a fitting location which is accessible for the user who "
"executes the restore script."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:130
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Configure Backup Script"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:134
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For a new installation, this is required. At least you have to provide a "
"directory where your backups are stored. See [Backup "
"Configuration](#backup-configuration) for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:135
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the Restore"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:141
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Be aware that restoring backups can overwrite your `database.yml`. You can\n"
"check that by looking into the `[...]_zammad_files.tar.gz` file. If there\n"
"is a `database.yml` in the directory *config > database*, ensure to save "
"the\n"
"original version **before restoring**.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:144
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The restore works in two possible ways, depending on how interactive you "
"want to go:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:145
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Interactive restore (recommended)\n"
"Run the script:\n"
"```bash\n"
"/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_restore.sh\n"
"```\n"
"Provide the requested information to the script and wait for the restore\n"
"process to finish. Depending on the size of your backup and host "
"performance,\n"
"this may take some time.\n"
"\n"
"=== Non-interactive restore\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:145
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only use the following option if you know what you're doing! The following\n"
"command will overwrite existing data without further prompts!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:145
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When called with a timestamp argument (matching the backups filename),\n"
"Zammad will proceed immediately to restoring the specified backup.\n"
"```bash\n"
"/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_restore.sh 20170507121848\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:170
#, markdown-text
msgid "The result should look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:171
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Zammad restore started - Fri Jan 21 17:54:13 CET 2022!\n"
"\n"
"The restore will delete your current database!\n"
"Be sure to have a backup available!\n"
"\n"
"Please ensure to have twice the storage of the uncompressed backup size!\n"
"\n"
"Note that the restoration USUALLY requires root permissions as services are "
"stopped!\n"
"\n"
"Enter 'yes' if you want to proceed!\n"
"Restore?: yes\n"
"Enter file date to restore:\n"
"20220120124714\n"
"20220121175344\n"
"File date: 20220121175344\n"
"Enter db date to restore:\n"
"20220120124714\n"
"20220121175344\n"
"DB date: 20220121175344\n"
"# Stopping Zammad\n"
"# Checking requirements\n"
"# ... Dropping current database zammad\n"
"Dropped database 'zammad'\n"
"# ... Creating database zammad for owner zammad\n"
"CREATE DATABASE\n"
"# Restoring PostgreSQL DB\n"
"# Restoring Files\n"
"# Ensuring correct file permissions ...\n"
"# Clearing Cache ...\n"
"# Starting Zammad\n"
"\n"
"# Zammad restored successfully - Fri Jan 21 17:54:34 CET 2022!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:214
#, markdown-text
msgid "If you've set any environmental settings, please re-apply them now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:214
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If not already done, [install "
"Elasticsearch](/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch) now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:214
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"[Connect Elasticsearch with Zammad and rebuild its search "
"index](/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch). The rebuild can safely "
"run during your work, but will cause a degraded search performance and may "
"lead to temporarily not found data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Connect and Configure Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:8
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Connect Elasticsearch with Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:10
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set the Elasticsearch URL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Set the Elasticsearch server address; adapt it to your scenario.\n"
"\n"
"# Elasticsearch 7:\n"
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_url', 'http://localhost:9200')\"\n"
"\n"
"# Elasticsearch 8:\n"
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_url', 'https://localhost:9200')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set the Elasticsearch User and Password <Badge type=\"warning\" text=\"only "
"ES8\" />"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Set Elasticsearch user and password\n"
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_user', 'elastic')\"\n"
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_password', '<password>')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Certificate to Zammad <Badge type=\"warning\" text=\"only ES8\" />"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Show and copy the auto-generated certificate from Elasticsearch and add it "
"to Zammad. Make sure to copy/paste the delimiters (e.g. `-----BEGIN "
"CERTIFICATE-----`) too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo cat /etc/elasticsearch/certs/http_ca.crt\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Go to the admin panel of Zammad and add your copied certificate under\n"
"*Settings > Security > SSL Certificates*.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Build/Rebuild the Searchindex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"zammad run rake zammad:searchindex:rebuild\n"
"\n"
"# Optionally, you can specify a number of CPU cores which are used for\n"
"# rebuilding the searchindex, as in the following example with 8 cores:\n"
"zammad run rake zammad:searchindex:rebuild[8]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optional Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We collected some useful settings you may want to apply. For further "
"information please have a look at [Elastic's "
"documentation](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Index Namespacing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Useful when connecting multiple services or Zammad instances to a single "
"Elasticsearch server (to prevent name collisions during indexing)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_index', Socket.gethostname.downcase + "
"'_zammad')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "File-Attachment Indexing Rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad supports searching in file attachments, which means Elasticsearch has "
"to index those, too. Limiting such indexing can help preserve system "
"resources."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Files with these extensions will not be indexed\n"
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_ignore',\\\n"
"[ '.png', '.jpg', '.jpeg', '.mpeg', '.mpg', '.mov', '.bin', '.exe', '.box', "
"'.mbox' ] )\"\n"
"\n"
"# Files larger than this size (in MB) will not be indexed\n"
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_max_size_in_mb', 50)\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Firewall & SELinux"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is just a collection of snippets which might be useful for you. Feel "
"free to skip parts and/or adapt it to your needs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Firewall"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following commands only work on Ubuntu, Debian and CentOS. If you use "
"a\n"
"different distribution, please have a look at their documentation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo chcon -Rv --type=httpd_sys_content_t /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo setsebool httpd_can_network_connect on -P\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo semanage fcontext -a -t httpd_sys_content_t /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo restorecon -Rv /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo chmod -R a+r /opt/zammad/public/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SELinux"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Ensure to open ports `80` and `443` (TCP & UDP) beside of the ports you "
"need. Below you can find a few examples for different distributions. If you "
"are using a different distribution, please have a look at their "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please note that the examples below only cover the distribution’s default "
"firewall. It may not cover your case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"===Ubuntu\n"
"```bash\n"
"$ sudo ufw allow 80\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"$ sudo ufw allow 443\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"$ sudo ufw reload\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"===Debian\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|info)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We’re covering `nftables` in this part - `iptables` is discouraged\n"
"starting from Debian 10 (Buster). Our example uses the `input` chain, "
"yours\n"
"may be a different one!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/firewall-selinux.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"Add the following lines to `/etc/nftables.conf` or your specific rule "
"file.\n"
"Ensure to add these lines to your input-chain.\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"sudo tcp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"sudo udp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"```\n"
"The result can look like the following. Keep in mind that your environment\n"
"could require different / more rules.\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"#!/usr/local/sbin/nft -f\n"
"flush ruleset\n"
"\n"
"table inet filter {\n"
"   chain input {\n"
"      type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;\n"
"      ct state established,related accept\n"
"      tcp dport ssh log accept\n"
"      tcp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"      udp dport { http, https } accept\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   chain forward {\n"
"      type filter hook forward priority 0; policy accept;\n"
"   }\n"
"\n"
"   chain output {\n"
"      type filter hook output priority 0; policy accept;\n"
"   }\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
"To load the rules, run:\n"
"```bash\n"
"sudo systemctl reload nftables\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"===CenOS, RHEL, OpenSUSE, SLES\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --add-service=http --permanent\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --zone=public --add-service=https --permanent\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"sudo firewall-cmd --reload\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

